<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Celaya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1915">1915</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexican-revolution">Mexican Revolution</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Celaya, in April 1915, was a pair of engagements near Celaya in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guanajuato">Guanajuato</a> in which Constitutionalist forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alvaro-obregon">Álvaro Obregón</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pancho-villa">Pancho Villa</a>'s Division of the North. Using trenches, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barbed-wire">barbed wire</a> and machine guns, Obregón broke repeated cavalry charges and inflicted heavy losses. The defeat ended Villa's bid for national power in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexican-revolution">Mexican Revolution</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-celaya.jpg" alt="Battle of Celaya" width="320" height="195" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Subido por Tatehuari el 14 de Marzo de 2007 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Batalla_celaya.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>After Madero’s murder in 1913, the Constitutionalists of Venustiano Carranza, Álvaro Obregón and Pancho Villa, together with the Zapatistas of Morelos, defeated Victoriano Huerta, and Obregón then beat Villa at the <b>battles of Celaya</b> in 1915.</blockquote><a href="/empire/mexico">Mexico · Military</a></li></ul></section>
